cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its report, please cite it as below."
title: "When the Container Is the Benchmark: A Bit-Exact Native Reimplementation of the ABIDES Market Simulator and What Whole-Container Timing Rewards"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Srivastava"
    given-names: "Shashwat"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: "1.3"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shashwat-srivastav/abides-native"
abstract: "A C++ reimplementation of the ABIDES agent-based market simulator that reproduces the Python reference's order trace and message ledger exactly, written for Agenthon 2026 Track 3, where the score is verified events divided by whole-container time. The repository holds the engine, a static launcher with its own Parquet writer, the validation and fuzzing tools, the complete laboratory record and a technical report. The best Development score reached is 203,394 events per container-second."
keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - market microstructure
  - ABIDES
  - bit-exact reproduction
  - benchmarking
  - performance engineering
